{"kind":"request","text":"Re-home the merge-artifact path guidance into the current documentation structure, because carrying the round-four work onto main left the rule without its walkthrough.\n\nDiscovered mid-flight while closing 3251a890 and recorded at 16eea7fa. The round-four branch was cut before main split docs/getting-started.md into docs/how-to and docs/reference and replaced docs/reference.md with a docs/reference/ directory. Its operative guidance lived in those two files, so carrying the branch forward without reverting the restructure meant taking main's versions and losing the prose.\n\nWhat is missing is the part that tells someone what to do. AGENTS.md now says to retire every live artifact covering what the merge changed and publish a successor at the path each area keeps, and it lists the four cases. What it does not carry is the walkthrough: how to ask git which paths a merge changed, how to read the exact strings the live artifacts already use out of `gs status`, and how to work each of the four cases with the commands in order. A contract that states a rule and gives no procedure is the shape that produced the dot-artifact problem in the first place — everyone reached for the one path that obviously worked.\n\nThe two homes are docs/how-to/end-to-end.md, which already walks a complete loop and stops before this step, and a reference page for `gs merge` under docs/reference/gs/. The how-to should carry the procedure; the reference should carry the rules and refusals. Neither should restate AGENTS.md, which is the contract rather than the manual.\n\nWorth stating for whoever takes it: the prose exists in git history at 556a5644 and does not need rewriting from nothing, but it does need re-cutting, because it was written for a single flat page and the two destinations have different jobs.","body":{"conditions":"The merge-artifact path procedure is present in the current documentation structure: docs/how-to/end-to-end.md carries the walkthrough — asking git which paths the merge changed, reading the exact live paths from `gs status`, and the commands for each of the four cases in order — and a `gs merge` reference page under docs/reference/gs/ carries the rules and what the command refuses; neither restates AGENTS.md, which stays the contract; the pages rest on the artifacts for the behaviour they describe rather than only on this request; the docset gates pass, including the anchor gate resolving every named act to a live artifact and the example execution running any `sh` blocks; `go vet` passes; reviewed by a different agent at an exact head before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}